(1) side conditions over 741 quadratic Pisot alpha>2, rho<1/2:
    min (diam K - gap_max C) = 0.051316   [M0's no-go 2, verbatim]
    min (diam C - gap_max K) = 0.001348
    both > 0 => whenever tau_C*tau_K >= 1, C-K IS an interval of length >= 2 => X = T

